    "wikipedia_summary": "<i><b>Cerastium fontanum</b></i>, also called <b>mouse-ear chickweed</b>, <b>common mouse-ear</b>, or <b>starweed</b>, is a species of mat-forming perennial or, rarely, annual plant. It is native to Europe but introduced elsewhere. Its identifying characteristics are tear-shaped leaves growing opposite one another in a star pattern, hairy leaves, and small white flowers. Mouse-ear chickweed typically grows to 4\"-8\" tall and spreads horizontally along the ground via the formation of roots wherever the stem falls over and contacts the ground.",
